  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 709.22 Coliform Assessment Triggers and Required Actions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 709.22 Coliform Assessment Triggers and Required Actions.\n\n(a) A PWS owner shall conduct an assessment in accordance with Env-Dw 720.07 if an assessment is triggered as specified in (b) or (c) below.\n\n(b) The level 1 assessment shall be triggered if:\n\n(1) For a PWS collecting fewer than 40 samples per month, the system has 2 or more total coliform-positive samples in the same month;\n\n(2) For a PWS collecting 40 or more samples per month, more than 5.0% of the samples collected during a month are total coliform-positive; or\n\n(3) The PWS fails to take every required repeat sample after any single total coliform-positive sample result.\n\n(c) The level 2 assessment shall be triggered if:\n\n(1) An E. coli MCL violation as specified in Env-Dw 702.02 occurs; or\n\n(2) A second level 1 assessment is triggered within 12 months of a prior level 1 or level 2 assessment, unless the department has:\n\na. Identified a likely reason that the samples that caused the first level 1 treatment technique trigger were total coliform-positive; and\n\nb. Determined that the owner has corrected the problem.\n\nSource. #10771, eff 2-1-15; ss by 14343, eff 8-22-25, EXPIRES: 8-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
}
